<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=windmill">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Energy and power</p><h1 class="enc-title">Windmill</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A windmill is a machine driven by wind acting on vanes or sails to grind grain or pump water, first known in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>, where windmills were working in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorasan">Khorasan</a> in the 9th century. These had sails turning around a vertical shaft and spread across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-east">Middle East</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, reaching southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> by the 11th century. The vertical windmill developed in north-western Europe in the 12th century, and the earliest certain reference to one in northern Europe dates from 1185, at Weedley in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yorkshire">Yorkshire</a>. Europe's windmills peaked at about 200,000 around 1850.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/windmill.jpg" alt="Windmill" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peter Broster · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moulin_de_la_Solitude_(8061957726).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>9th century</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Khorasan, Persia</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Whether the vertical windmill of 12th-century Europe owed anything to the Persian one is unclear.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/sail">Sail<span>6th millennium BCE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/water-wheel">Water wheel<span>4th century BCE</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=windmill">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
